The area of interest (AOI) was projected to UTM Zone 36S (EPSG:32736) and partitioned into a regular lattice of 500 × 500 m grid cells. Grid cells were intersected with the AOI boundary. The AOI centroid was used to subdivide the grid into four quadrants (NW, NE, SW, SE), with each grid cell assigned to a quadrant from its centroid. Using seed 42, a stratified random sample of 2 NW, 2 NE, 3 SW, and 3 SE cells was selected as an independent holdout region; all remaining cells were assigned to model development. Raster tiles inherited a development or holdout designation from the grid cell containing the tile centroid. The preserved experiment contains 804 development and 222 validation image-mask pairs, with no duplicate filenames or grid cells shared between sets. The selected SE holdout cells contain no image-tile centroids, so the 222 validation tiles themselves occur in the NW, NE, and SW quadrants. The saved grid and tile manifest provide the authoritative record of this published split.
